<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nilambar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. late 15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nilambar was the last king of the Khen dynasty of Kamata, ruling from Kamatapur near modern Cooch Behar in the late 15th century. He controlled a large territory between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karatoya-river">Karatoya</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a> and resisted the Bengal Sultanate, but around 1498 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-husain-shah">Alauddin Husain Shah</a> captured Kamatapur, ending the dynasty. Local legends remember him as a great king.</p></div>
